1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:04,920
Who wants the last dumpling?

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:05,610
Ooh, me!

3
00:00:05,610 --> 00:00:07,600
Penny, a moment.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,810
We just had Thai food.

5
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:12,570
In that culture, the last morsel is called

6
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:15,790
the "Greng Jai" piece, and it is reserved for

7
00:00:15,790 --> 00:00:19,400
the most important and valued member of the group.

8
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:27,850
Thank you all for this high honor.

9
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:32,680
I've seen pictures of your mother, keep eating.

10
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:41,090
All right, honey, if we're gonna make the movie, we should go.

11
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:46,260
This may be hard for you to hear,

12
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:50,350
but when I say "honey," I mean my fiance.

13
00:00:51,830 --> 00:00:53,890
Yeah, well, now it means her.

14
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:58,790
It's okay if he wants to come.

15
00:00:58,790 --> 00:01:01,160
Fine. But next time, we get a sitter.

16
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,340
All right, I got to go to work.

17
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:05,340
- I'll walk down with you.  - Wait.

18
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:08,340
Which is closer to the new train store in Monrovia,

19
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:11,260
the movie theater or The Cheesecake Factory?

20
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:12,650
Neither of them are close.

21
00:01:12,650 --> 00:01:13,640
Oh, well, then I guess it doesn't matter

22
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,560
which one of you drives me.

23
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:17,350
Let's play a fun guessing game

24
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:18,750
to see who gets to take me.

25
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:22,160
All right, this four-letter word describes either

26
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:26,760
a printer's type size or a compulsion to eat dirt.

27
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:27,910
Okay, I'm not driving him.

28
00:01:27,910 --> 00:01:30,090
Penny, don't give up, you can get this.

29
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,320
Aren't you going with Sheldon?

30
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:39,190
No, I have no interest in model trains,

31
00:01:39,190 --> 00:01:42,400
stores that sell them, nor their heartbreaking clientele.

32
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:47,690
Well, I have some work to do, so...

33
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:48,970
I can't imagine that would disturb me.

34
00:01:48,970 --> 00:01:50,330
Carry on.

35
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:53,390
Okay.

36
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,550
Wouldn't you be more comfortable at home?

37
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:01,980
Not really, no.

38
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:05,480
All righty then.

39
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,660
Guess I'll just get started.

40
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:08,940
Leonard, please. I don't need the running commentary.

41
00:02:53,350 --> 00:02:54,920
- Amy?   - Yo.

42
00:02:56,590 --> 00:02:57,450
You okay?

43
00:02:57,450 --> 00:02:59,040
Oh, sure.

44
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,220
I thought you were reading.

45
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:04,360
I was.

46
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:06,820
Now I'm thinking about what I read.

47
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:20,410
You all right, Leonard?

48
00:03:20,410 --> 00:03:22,380
You seem very uncomfortable.

49
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:25,110
I-I'm fine.

50
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:27,660
Should I go?

51
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:30,520
I've been told sometimes I overstay my welcome.

52
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:33,060
Wha... who told you that?

53
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:37,530
Well, most recently my gynecologist.

54
00:03:42,690 --> 00:03:45,130
Well, you stay as long as you'd like.

55
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:47,210
I'm glad to hear you say that,

56
00:03:47,210 --> 00:03:49,570
because I'm having a wonderful time.

57
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:54,310
I said the same thing to my gynecologist.

58
00:03:59,410 --> 00:04:01,720
What are you going to get at the train store, Sheldon?

59
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:03,630
Oh, I'm not buying anything.

60
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:05,830
They're having a lecture.

61
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:07,800
"H-O gauge railroading.

62
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:11,530
Half the size of O-gauge, but twice the fun."

63
00:04:12,230 --> 00:04:14,330
Very controversial topic.

64
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,130
Which side do you come down on?

65
00:04:17,130 --> 00:04:18,730
I'll let you know after tonight.

66
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:21,900
Unlike some people, I'm going in with an open mind.

67
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:23,420
Who am I kidding?

68
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:26,260
Of course we all know it's O-gauge or no gauge.

69
00:04:27,230 --> 00:04:31,680
Can you believe grown men sit around and play with toy trains?

70
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,760
That's pretty big talk for a man

71
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:36,140
with a closet full of magic tricks at his mother's house.

72
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:40,400
First of all, they're not tricks, they're illusions.

73
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,960
And...

74
00:04:42,810 --> 00:04:44,760
secondly, when we get married, they're all going up

75
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:48,740
in the attic so you can have that closet for clothes.

76
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:51,340
Why would I keep clothes at your mother's house?

77
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:52,390
Well, don't think of it that way.

78
00:04:52,390 --> 00:04:55,020
Once we move in, it'll be our house.

79
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:56,330
Is she moving out?

80
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:56,980
Why would she move out?

81
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,610
It's her house.

82
00:05:00,710 --> 00:05:01,680
Hang on.

83
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:04,170
You seriously think I'm going to live with your mother?

84
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:05,940
Howard, I think I can help here.

85
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:09,220
Yes, Bernadette, that's exactly what he thinks.

86
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:10,430
Why not?

87
00:05:10,430 --> 00:05:12,290
It's a great house, plenty of room,

88
00:05:12,290 --> 00:05:14,260
and if we have kids, Mom's there to help.

89
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,410
You know, when she tells "The Three Little Pigs" story,

90
00:05:16,410 --> 00:05:19,750
she actually has hair on her chinny-chin-chin.

91
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:22,770
I'm not gonna live with your mother.

92
00:05:22,770 --> 00:05:25,670
Not now, not ever.

93
00:05:25,670 --> 00:05:29,330
Wow, someone obviously has some mommy issues.

94
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:32,710
Raj, take me home.

95
00:05:32,710 --> 00:05:34,990
Don't listen to her. Go to the movie theater.

96
00:05:34,990 --> 00:05:36,470
Take me home now.

97
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:38,240
Movie theater!

98
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,810
Okay, everybody calm down.

99
00:05:40,810 --> 00:05:42,470
There is a simple solution here.

100
00:05:42,470 --> 00:05:44,530
Raj, take me to the train store,

101
00:05:44,530 --> 00:05:47,320
and then I don't care what you people do.

102
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:55,540
How was your shower?

103
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:58,300
It was good, good.

104
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:01,990
Just out of curiosity, what time do you usually go to bed?

105
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:03,070
Oh, I'm up all night.

106
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:05,050
I'm like a possum.

107
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:10,130
Boy, you were not liked in high school, were you?

108
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:11,350
Not really.

109
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:13,390
Is that my yearbook?

110
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:15,440
"Dear Leonard, you're really good at science.

111
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:16,500
Maybe one day you'll come up

112
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,600
with a cure for being a dork".

113
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,590
Well, it wasn't spray-painting a Lightning Bolt

114
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:24,090
on my briefcase, I can tell you that.

115
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,190
If it makes you feel any better,

116
00:06:26,190 --> 00:06:28,740
the only person who signed my yearbook was my mother.

117
00:06:29,690 --> 00:06:30,730
"Dear Amy,

118
00:06:30,730 --> 00:06:32,750
self-respect and a hymen are better than friends and fun.

119
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:34,670
Love, Mom".

120
00:06:36,210 --> 00:06:38,580
Well, you can add Jerry's Junction

121
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:40,220
to the list of train stores

122
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:43,120
Sheldon Cooper will never set foot in again.

123
00:06:43,810 --> 00:06:46,280
Rough night, Casey Jones?

124
00:06:47,010 --> 00:06:48,280
You don't know the half of it.

125
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,680
It was billed as a lively give-and-take

126
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,610
on the merits of model train sizes.

127
00:06:52,610 --> 00:06:54,990
But it was actually a setup to intimidate

128
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:58,690
weak-minded spineless rubes into buying H-O starter sets.

129
00:06:58,690 --> 00:06:59,980
What's in the bag?

130
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:01,940
I don't want to talk about it.

131
00:07:03,270 --> 00:07:06,010
But it's not a spine, I'll tell you that.

132
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:08,510
Well, I had a delightful evening, Leonard.

133
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:09,840
We should do this again sometime.

134
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:11,790
Ah, sure. That'd be nice.

135
00:07:12,210 --> 00:07:13,140
Glad to hear it.

136
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:14,760
I need someone to accompany me to the wedding

137
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:17,620
of Dr. Moranelli and Dr. Gustufson this Friday.

138
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:18,850
They're kind of the Brad and Angelina

139
00:07:18,850 --> 00:07:20,960
of the primatology department.

140
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,880
Wouldn't you rather bring Sheldon?

141
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:25,830
I would, but the last wedding we went to was a disaster.

142
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:28,220
He behaved like a child the entire time.

143
00:07:28,220 --> 00:07:29,190
Not my fault.

144
00:07:29,190 --> 00:07:32,120
You said there'd be other scientists there my age.

145
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:38,450
Doesn't matter. You're out, he's in.

146
00:07:38,450 --> 00:07:39,410
No date to the prom,

147
00:07:39,410 --> 00:07:40,680
two dates to a wedding.

148
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,820
Hmm, how times change.

149
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:49,910
Ha-ha, you have to go to a wedding.

150
00:07:54,550 --> 00:07:55,670
I'll get it!

151
00:07:55,670 --> 00:07:56,720
Could you get it?!

152
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,280
I just said I'm getting it!

153
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,540
Fine, I'll get it!

154
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:01,410
I got it!

155
00:08:06,370 --> 00:08:08,050
I don't want to fight.

156
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:09,520
I was just surprised when you sprung

157
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:12,150
the whole living-with-your-mom stuff on me.

158
00:08:12,150 --> 00:08:16,100
Yeah, well, I'm sorry I didn't run it by you first.

159
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:17,650
I don't know who you're talking to,

160
00:08:17,650 --> 00:08:19,030
but in or out!

161
00:08:19,030 --> 00:08:21,190
We don't need bugs!

162
00:08:22,490 --> 00:08:24,370
The bugs only come here

163
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:27,290
because you're their queen!

164
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:31,870
Listen, how about this.

165
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:33,480
Before we make any kind of decision

166
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:35,460
about where we live, we have a trial run.

167
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:38,370
Stay here for a weekend, see what it's like.

168
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:40,040
And your mom would be okay with that?

169
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:40,930
Sure she would.

170
00:08:40,930 --> 00:08:43,820
Ma, do you mind if Bernadette stays here this weekend?!

171
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:46,550
Hey, if she's willing to give the milk away for free,

172
00:08:46,550 --> 00:08:48,700
who am I to say no?!

173
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,160
See? She's good with it.

174
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:56,260
Frankly, after all your sleepovers

175
00:08:56,260 --> 00:09:00,850
with the little brown boy, a girl is a big relief!

176
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:13,410
All these years, I've been so wrong.

177
00:09:13,410 --> 00:09:17,760
The tinier the train, the more concentrated the fun.

178
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:23,310
You're a brain scientist.

179
00:09:23,310 --> 00:09:24,840
Can you explain to me why a brilliant man

180
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,830
likes playing with toy trains?

181
00:09:26,830 --> 00:09:29,210
Not without cutting his head open, no.

182
00:09:30,630 --> 00:09:33,070
How about making my eyes like Cleopatra?

183
00:09:33,070 --> 00:09:35,060
Really? For a wedding?

184
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:36,260
Perhaps you're right.

185
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:37,860
My cheekbones and beckoning pelvis

186
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:40,980
already have a certain "hello sailor" quality to them.

187
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:43,560
Ready.

188
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,840
So handsome.

189
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,170
Like James Bond.

190
00:09:49,170 --> 00:09:53,810
He's better than James Bond, because he's tinier.

191
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:57,460
I got you this to give to me.

192
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:00,430
Oh, sweetie, guests don't normally

193
00:10:00,430 --> 00:10:01,900
wear corsages to a wedding.

194
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:03,580
That's more of a prom thing.

195
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:04,950
I never went to my prom.

196
00:10:04,950 --> 00:10:06,490
My mom paid my cousin to take me,

197
00:10:06,490 --> 00:10:08,870
but he just used the money to buy drugs.

198
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:12,520
Put the corsage on her.

199
00:10:15,090 --> 00:10:17,200
Amy, this is for you.

200
00:10:18,890 --> 00:10:21,720
When you're done copping a feel, that goes on my wrist.

201
00:10:24,490 --> 00:10:28,300
All aboard!

202
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:30,350
It's official.

203
00:10:30,350 --> 00:10:33,430
I'm an H-O trainiac.

204
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:38,860
So, dinner went nice.

205
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:41,090
Yeah. Yeah, I guess.

206
00:10:41,870 --> 00:10:44,750
Does your mother always cut your meat for you?

207
00:10:46,910 --> 00:10:49,030
Only when it's fatty.

208
00:10:50,090 --> 00:10:51,710
Well, don't be jealous, babe.

209
00:10:51,710 --> 00:10:54,450
Someday you'll get to cut it for me.

210
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:56,100
Bernadette!

211
00:10:56,100 --> 00:11:00,370
I found the extra head for the Waterpik if you want to use it!

212
00:11:00,370 --> 00:11:02,260
I'm okay, Mrs. Wolowitz.

213
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:03,200
You sure?!

214
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:06,840
I just squirted half a brisket outta my teeth!

215
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:09,800
Hey, Ma, how about a little privacy?!

216
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:12,120
Oh, I know what that means!

217
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:14,340
Hubba-hubba!

218
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,910
Oh, God.

219
00:11:15,910 --> 00:11:17,810
Relax, it'll be fine.

220
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,890
Okay.

221
00:11:19,890 --> 00:11:22,600
Let me know when you're done canoodling!

222
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:25,460
Mommy needs a foot rub!

223
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,750
Would you like to dance?

224
00:11:43,750 --> 00:11:44,580
No, thank you.

225
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:46,560
I'm really not much of a dancer.

226
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:49,630
You're not exactly winning any trophies

227
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:51,740
as a conversationalist, either.

228
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,570
I'm sorry.

229
00:11:56,890 --> 00:11:58,750
The bride and groom seem happy.

230
00:11:58,750 --> 00:12:00,220
Why shouldn't they be?

231
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,280
They have a feverish night of

232
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:04,490
socially-approved copulation ahead of them.

233
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,880
In some cultures, we'd stand outside of their bedroom

234
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:10,570
cheering as they achieved orgasm.

235
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:12,890
That sounds like a late night,

236
00:12:12,890 --> 00:12:15,040
and I have work in the morning, so...

237
00:12:16,370 --> 00:12:17,780
Leonard, you may not have noticed,

238
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:20,140
but I am being a delight here.

239
00:12:21,140 --> 00:12:23,620
And you're not holding up your end of the evening.

240
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:26,140
Oh, sorry. This wedding just reminds me

241
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:29,830
of my kinda-sorta girlfriend 9,000 miles away.

242
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:32,590
I have a kinda-sorta boyfriend who's playing with a model train right now,

243
00:12:32,590 --> 00:12:34,760
 you don't hear me bitching about it.

244
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:41,000
Leonard, a word of advice-- moody self-obsession

245
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,970
is only attractive in men who can play guitar

246
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:45,720
and are considerably taller than you.

247
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,110
I'm not moody.

248
00:12:47,110 --> 00:12:48,560
I'm fun.

249
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,940
You have any evidence to support that statement?

250
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:54,280
Well, hey, I'm just as much fun as you are.

251
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:57,140
Really? Are you willing to draw a mustache on your finger

252
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:59,570
as a conversational icebreaker?

253
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:02,100
I am.

254
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:07,560
Okay, fine, what do you suggest?

255
00:13:09,210 --> 00:13:10,850
We just had a lovely meal,

256
00:13:10,850 --> 00:13:14,050
the band... is on fire...

257
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:16,360
and you're sitting next to a beautiful woman

258
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:18,320
wearing whorish makeup.

259
00:13:19,790 --> 00:13:21,780
Why don't we head out on the dance floor

260
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:24,430
and see if I can sweat through these dress shields.

261
00:13:25,150 --> 00:13:27,830
Once again, I-I'm really not much of a dancer.

262
00:13:27,830 --> 00:13:29,480
Don't worry...

263
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:31,580
I'll lead.

264
00:13:36,530 --> 00:13:40,060
("The Chicken Dance" playing)

265
00:14:02,950 --> 00:14:04,510
Howard?

266
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,190
Ready for bed?

267
00:14:08,190 --> 00:14:10,290
No. I need to brush my teeth, but your mother's

268
